<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

</div>

<span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Times New Roman","serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;
mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA'><br
clear=all style='page-break-before:right;mso-break-type:section-break'>
</span>

<div class=Section8>

<p class=MsoHeading7><a name="_Toc251442693"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>D<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Annex
D: String Library</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The string library implements various useful string
functions. Strings are built out of arrays of characters in Pascal, and
extended in Pascaline. <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>strlib</span></span> unifies two
schemes. The first is the space padded right scheme familiar from standard
Pascal. The second is dynamic strings.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Dynamic strings are almost the ideal string type. They are
unlimited in length, they can be returned from a function. And because their
storage is recycled, they are space efficient. They can also be fairly speed
efficient by managing when and if they are recycled.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The declarations for padded or fixed, and dynamic strings
appear as:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code>type string = packed array of char;</p>

<p class=code><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>     </span>pstring = ^string;</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The string functions are often overloaded so that they take
both types of strings.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442694"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>D.1<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Conventions</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>In some cases, it is ambiguous whether a padded or dynamic string
argument is meant. For example, the string compare facility does not know which
type its operands are, and it makes a difference to the result, since length
plays a part in string comparison. For these situations, a &quot;p&quot; (for
padded) is appended to the name of the procedure or function.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Many functions and procedures must know if case matters. For
example, string compare can be with case, or caseless. For these procedures and
functions, there is appended a &quot;c&quot; to the ones that case does matter.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>A few functions and procedures perform different actions on
strings vs. characters. For the string versions, an &quot;s&quot; is appended
to the name.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442695"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>D.2<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Words</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Some of the functions and procedures treat the strings as a
series of words. Words are a series of non-space characters surrounded by one
or more spaces. For example:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='mso-tab-count:1'>            </span>‘<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>hi<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>   </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>there<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>                   </span>George<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>             </span>‘</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Has three words, 'hi', 'there', and 'george'. Such words can
be counted, indexed and extracted.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442696"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>D.3<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Format
Strings</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Some routines accept a &quot;format string&quot; to output
numbers with. The format is an image of the output string the number is
converted into. The string will contain a series of format characters. The
entire format string is copied to the result string, but the special format
characters are replaced with parts of the number to be converted.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The number “image” contained within the format string
consists of from 0 to any number of leading spaces, followed by any number of
trailing spaces. The spaces are significant, and will appear in the result.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The first thing the format routines do is match the format
to the number for decimal point position. For example:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>+999,999.999<span style='mso-tab-count:2'>      </span>Format characters</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>         </span>50.12<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>        </span>Actual number</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Then, the meaning of each format character depends on if
that character appears to the left or to the right of the decimal point. There
can only be one decimal point in the format string, or it is an error.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Each format character operates on the digit that matches
it’s position after decimal point alignment.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The format characters are:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>9</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Represents a digit. To the left
of the decimal point, this is replaced with it’s matching digit from the number.
If there is no digit in the number at that position, a space replaces the format
character. To the right of the decimal point, if the digit position is
non-zero, or there are non-zero digits to the right, the digit replaces the
format character,otherwise space.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>0</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>As &quot;9&quot; above, but
&quot;0&quot; replaces the digit if no significant digit is found, instead of
space when to the left of the decimal point. To the right of the decimal point,
if the digit position is non-zero, then it replaces the format character,
otherwise remains 0.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>-</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Represents the sign. To the left
of the decimal pont, if the number is negative, it is left alone. If the number
is positive, it is replaced by a space. If the sign was already output, then it
is replaced by space. It is an error if this format character is used to the
right of the decimal point.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>+</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>As &quot;-&quot;, but
&quot;+&quot; appears instead of space on a positive number.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>$, &amp;, %</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>These characters are used to
indicate if the number is hex (or USA dollars), octal or binary. To the left of
the decimal point, if a significant digit can be matched to this position, that
is output, otherwise, either the character, or a space is placed. The space is placed
if any of the format characters ‘$’, ‘&amp;’, or ‘%’ have already appeared. It
is an error if this format character is used to the right of the decimal point.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>,</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>To the left of the decimal point,
if the comma appears to the right of any non-zero significant digits, it is output
as is. Otherwise, it is either replaced by space. If a &quot;$&quot;,
&quot;&amp;&quot; or &quot;%&quot; character appears to the left of it, it will
be replaced by that. It is an error if this format character is used to the
right of the decimal point.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:28.8pt'>May only appear on real numbers.
This format character is always printed, but specifies where the mantissa of a
number appears, and where its fraction appears. The appearance of the decimal
point will enable or disable the fraction. If present, fractional digits are
output, otherwise, the fraction is discarded.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442697"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>D.4<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Recycling</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>By default, <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>strlib</span></span>
leaves it up to the programmer to determine when dynamic strings should be recycled.
To keep from losing space (&quot;memory leaks&quot;), the program must be
careful to keep track of all dynamic strings created, and return them to free
storage via dispose.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>Strlib</span></span> can use
a nested blocking system to automatically dispose of strings for you. The <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>openstring</span></span> call begins a new
string block, and <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>closestring</span></span>
ends it. When a new block is opened, any dynamic strings allocated are recorded
in the block. Then, each of them are disposed of when the block ends. Any
number of block levels can exist. With no blocks in effect, the automatic
recycling system is off, which is the state <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>strlib</span></span>
starts in. When all blocks are closed, <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>strlib</span></span>
reverts to this state. Because the dynamic strings are returned as a group, this
system can be more efficient than returning the strings one at a time.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>Exportstring</span></span> to
completely remove a given dynamic string from the automated recycling system. The
<span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>upstring</span></span> call takes a string, and
moves it to the surrounding string block.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>strlib</span></span> block
system has nothing to do with blocks in Pascal. <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>strlib</span></span>
blocks can cross blocks, functions and even whole modules of Pascal. The two
are entirely unrelated.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><![if !supportLists]><span style='mso-fareast-font-family:
Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:none;text-underline:none'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>D.5<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Exceptions</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The following exceptions are generated in <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>strlib</span></span>:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>NoStringBlock<span
style='mso-tab-count:3'>                         </span>No string block is
active.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>OuterBlockFull<span
style='mso-tab-count:3'>                                    </span>No room in
outermost string block.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>CurrentBlockFull<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>                     </span>Current string block is
full.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>StringNil<span
style='mso-tab-count:3'>                                  </span>String passed
is nil.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>StringDestinationOverflow<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>      </span>String was to large for destination.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>IndexOutOfRange<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>                   </span>String index out of range.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>NegativeRepeatCount<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>              </span>Repeat count was negative.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>WordIndexOutOfRange<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>                       </span>Word array index was out
of range.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>StringReadOverflow<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>                </span>String was too large to read.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>FormatTooLarge<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>                      </span>Format is too large for
destination</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>InvalidFieldSpecification<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>         </span>Field specified is invalid</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>NegativeValueNondecimal<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>      </span>Radix was negative</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>NumberOverflowsFormat<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>        </span>Number overflows space provided in
format string.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>NegativeNotPlaced<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>                  </span>Negative sign not placed in
format.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>InvalidRealNumber<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>                 </span>Invalid real number.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>InvalidFractionSpecification<span
style='mso-tab-count:1'>    </span>Invalid fraction specification.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>InvalidRadix<span
style='mso-tab-count:3'>                            </span>Invalid radix</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>InvalidIntegerFormat<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>               </span>Invalid integer format.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>NumberTooLarge<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>                    </span>Number too large.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>IntegerTooLarge<span
style='mso-tab-count:2'>                      </span>Integer too large.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>InvalidRealFormat<span style='mso-tab-count:2'>                   </span>Invalid
real format.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>Strlib</span></span>
establishes a series of exception handlers for each of the above exceptions
during startup. Exceptions not handled by a client program of <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>strlib</span></span> will go back to <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>strlib</span></span>, then print a message
specific to the error, then the general exception will be thrown.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Not all procedures and functions throw all exceptions. See
each procedure or function description for a list of exceptions thrown. A
client of <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>strlib</span></span> need only capture the
exceptions occurring in the procedure or function that is called.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442698"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>D.6<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Procedures
and functions in strlib</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function lcase(c: char):
char;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function lcase(s: pstring): pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function lcases(s: string):
pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure lcases(s: string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the
lower case version of a character <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>
or string <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>. This is either returned, or
converted in place.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Exceptions:
StringNil</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function ucase(c: char):
char;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function ucase(s: pstring):
pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function ucases(s: string):
pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure ucases(s: string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the
upper case version of a character <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>
or string <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>. This is either returned, or
converted in place.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Exceptions:
StringNil</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure clears(var s:
string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Clears string
<span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> to all spaces. To set an entire
string to another character value besides space, use <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>rep</span></span> below.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function len(s: [p]string):
integer;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the
padded length of a string <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>. This is
equivalent to the index of the last non-space character, or zero if there is
none. Note that dynamic string lengths are found via the system function <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>max</span></span>. </p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Exceptions:
StringNil</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure copy(var d: string;
s: [p]string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function copy(s: [p]string):
pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure copy(var d:
pstring; s: string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Create a
copy of the source <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> string in the
destination <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>d</span></span> or returns it as a result. If
the destination is a fixed string, then it will be padded on the right with
spaces to fill it out. If the destination or return type is dynamic, then a new
string will be created of the same length as the source, and the source copied
to that. In the case of the last procedure, the source is taken to be a padded
string, and the length is without padding. This procedure is used to copy from
a padded string to a dynamic string.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Exceptions:
StringNil, StringDestinationOverflow</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure cat(var d: string; s:
string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function cat(sa: [p]string;
sb:[p]string): pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Concatenate
two strings <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>d</span></span> and <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>,
or <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sa</span></span> and <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sb</span></span>. For the first procedure, the
padded destination and source are concatenated into the padded destination. The
function concatenates unpadded strings to a dynamic result.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>When
concatenating two padded strings, it is not possible using cat to concatenate
with a space or spaces between strings. For this case, use a padded string
insert instead, with the source string inserted after the desired number of
spaces.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Exceptions:
StringNil, StringDestinationOverflow</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function comp[c](sa: [p]string;
sb: [p]string): boolean;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function comp[c]p(sa, sb:string):
boolean;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Compare
strings <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sa</span></span> and <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sb</span></span>. Returns true if the strings
are equal. Compares case or caseless, and padded or fixed length. Strings are
equal only if they have the same length and content.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Exceptions:
StringNil</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function gtr[c](sa: [p]string;
sb: [p]string): boolean;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function gtr[c]p(sa, sb:string):
boolean;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Compare
string <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sb</span></span> is greater than string <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sa</span></span>. Returns true if the second
string is greater than the first. Compares case or caseless, and padded or
fixed length. Strings are compared from left to right, until the first
difference is found. Then, the second string is greater than the first if the
ord of its character is greater than the first. In case one string is longer
than the other, but otherwise equal, the shorter string is less than the longer
string.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>This function
can be used to find less than, greater than or equal, and less than or equal by
arranging the operands:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>gtr(a, b)<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>      </span>a &lt; b</p>

<p class=code style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>gtr(b, a)<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>      </span>a &gt; b</p>

<p class=code style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>not gtr(a,
b)<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>a &gt;= b</p>

<p class=code style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>not gtr(b,
a)<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>a &lt;= b</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Exceptions:
StringNil</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function index[c](sa: [p]string;
sb: [p]string): integer;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function index[c]p(sa, sb:string):
integer;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the incidence
of the source string <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sb</span></span> in the string
<span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sa</span></span>. If the source string is found
within the destination, the index of its first character is returned, otherwise
0. The comparison may be case or caseless. The padded versions are for when the
source string is padded.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Exceptions:
StringNil</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure extract(var d: string;
s: string; l, r: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function extract(s: [p]string;
l, r: integer): pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Extract a
substring. The source string <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> from the left
index to the right index is extracted, and either placed in the destination <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>d</span></span>, or returned. It is an error if
either index is out of range, but indexes l &gt; r simply result in a null string.
If the result is too large for the destination, an error results. The procedure
version is for padded strings.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Common
equivalents using extract are:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>right(s,l)<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>extract(s,max(s)-l+1,max(s))<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>Get right string</p>

<p class=code style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>left(s,l)<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>   </span>extract(s,1,l)<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>                </span>Get<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>left string</p>

<p class=code style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>mid(s,l,r)<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>extract(s,l,l+r-1)<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>            </span>Get mid string</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Exceptions:
StringNil, StringDestinationOverflow, IndexOutOfRange</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure insert(var d: string;
s: string; p: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function insert(sa:[p]string;
sb: [p]string; p: integer): pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Inserts a
substring from the source <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> into the
destination <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>d</span></span>. The procedure version is for
padded strings. If the source string is too long for the destination, an error
results.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function rep(s: [p]string; r:
integer): pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure rep(var d: string;
s:string; r: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Repeats
the source string <span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>r</span></span>
times into the destination <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>d</span></span> or the return
string. The procedure version is for padded strings. If the resulting string is
too long for the destination, an error results.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function trim(s: [p]string):
pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure trim(var d: string;
s: string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Trim leading
and trailing spaces from string <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>.
and returns the result in string <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>d</span></span>
or the result The procedure version is for padded strings. For padded strings,
only the leading spaces are affected.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function words(s: [p]string):
integer;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Returns a
count of the number of space delimited words in the string <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function extwords(s: [p]string;
l, r: integer): pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure extwords(var d:
string; s: string; l, r: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Extracts
the space delimited words from the string <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>,
between the left to the right indicies inclusive. Returns the result in <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>d</span></span> or as the result.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure reads([f: text;]
var s: [p]string [; var ovf: boolean]);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Reads a
line to string <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> from text
file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>. The versions of this procedure
that have an <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>ovf</span></span> flag return it true if the
input line overflowed the string. In this case, the string is returned
truncated to the left. The non-<span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>ovf</span></span>
versions of the procedure <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>halt</span></span> with error
on overflow.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If the
input file is not specified, then the standard <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>input</span></span>
file is used.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure ints(var s: string;
i: integer [; fl: integer] | [fmt: string]);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function ints(i: integer [; fl:
integer] | [fmt: string]): pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Convert
integer <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>i</span></span> to string <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>. The versions with a field <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>fl</span></span> format the number using the field
using standard Pascal rules for output using a field. Negative (left justified)
fields are also allowed.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>The
versions with a <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>fmt</span></span> string copy
the format string into the result string, then replace each of the format
characters with parts of the number. See &quot;format strings&quot; in the main
text.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure reals(var s:
string; r: real [; f: integer] | [; fl: integer; fr: integer] | [; fmt:
string]);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function reals(r: real[; f:
integer] | [; fl: integer; fr: integer] | [; fmt: string]): pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Convert real
<span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>r</span></span> to string <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> with fraction <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>. The versions with a field <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>fl</span></span> format the number using the field
using standard Pascal rules for output using a field. Negative (left justified)
fields are also allowed.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>The versions
with a <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>fmt</span></span> string copy the format string
into the result string, then replace each of the format characters with parts
of the number. See &quot;format strings&quot; in the main text.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure reales(var s:
string; r: real [; fl: integer]);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function reales(r: real [; fl:
integer]): pstring;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Convert
real <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>r</span></span> to string <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> using &quot;economy&quot;
format. The real is printed in the minimum number of characters possible. If
the decimal position can be placed into the number, then it is, and the
exponent is removed. All insignificant leading and trailing zeros are removed,
and if there are no digits to the right or left of the decimal point, then that
is removed.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If the
decimal point cannot be placed into the number with less total characters than
a full ISO 7185 floating point number format, then the standard floating point
format is used.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>The versions
of this call with a field <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>fl</span></span> fit the
result into the field by padding it out with blanks, either on the left for
positive fields, or on the right for negative fields. If the number does not fit
into the specified field, then all of the required parts of the number are
printed. Note that if the ISO 7185 floating point number is chosen as the
shortest length number, then the rules for fields are identical to that of
normal real output formats.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

