<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure writed([var f: text;]
i: integer; fmt: string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Convert
integer <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>i</span></span> to character format and output
to file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, using the decimal radix
system. Decimal numbers are well covered by the normal ISO 7185 standard write
formats. However, these routines add image formatting to them.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>The versions
with a <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>fmt</span></span> string copy the format string
into the result string, then replace each of the format characters with parts
of the number. See &quot;format strings&quot; in the main text.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If the
output file is not specified, then the standard output file is used.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure writer([var f:
text;] r: real; fmt: string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Convert real
r to string s. Real numbers are well covered by the normal ISO 7185 standard
write formats. However, these routines add image formatting to them.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>The versions
with a <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>fmt</span></span> string copy the format string
into the result string, then replace each of the format characters with parts
of the number. See &quot;format strings&quot; in the main text.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If the
output file is not specified, then the standard output file is used.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure writere(var f:
text; r: real; fl: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure writere(r: real;
fl: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure writere(var f: text;
r: real);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure writere(r: real);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Write real
<span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>r</span></span> to the &quot;economy real&quot;
format to either the specified output file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>,
or to the standard output. The economy real format is explained in the <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>reales</span></span> routines descriptions.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>The
versions with a field <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>fl</span></span> fit the
output to the field using standard Pascal rules, including negative fields.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If the
output file is not specified, then the standard output file is used.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

