etdell, etdelcf, etdelcb, etcopy,<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span lang=FR style='mso-ansi-language:
FR'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>     </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>etcopyl, etcan, etstop, etcont, etprint,
etprintb, etprints,<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span lang=FR style='mso-ansi-language:
FR'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>     </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span></span>etmenu, etterm: (); { normal events }</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>{ <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>end</b> }</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>end</b>;</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The next event for the program is retrieved via the <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>event</span></span> call. The basis of the event
system is that events must be retrieved often enough that the input queue does
not fill up. Thus, an &quot;event model&quot; program will be centered around the
event loop that gets the next event, acts on it, and returns to the top for
more events.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442709"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>E.10<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Timers</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Timers allow a <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>trmlib</span></span>
program to perform periodic events, such as screen updates, and keeping track
of time. From 1 to 10 timers are available, numbered 1..10. Each timer is given
a time to measure, in 100 Microsecond counts (see <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>extlib</span></span>
for more details). When the timer is done, it sends an event to the event queue.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Timers can either simply stop when their time is done, or
they can automatically start timing their original set time again. This is the &quot;recurrent&quot;
mode, and it's useful when an activity needs to be performed periodically for
the life of the program. For example, updating the screen on an active program,
or checking when to update a clock display.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Timers are set by timer. A timer can be stopped or
&quot;killed&quot; by <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>killtimer</span></span>. Killing
a timer that is not active will not generate an error. This allows a single run
timer to be killed without worrying if it will time out during the call.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>It is important to understand that due to the queuing nature
of the event system, there is no guarantee about the accuracy of a timer. It
can arrive later than its set time. If the program is late getting back to the
event queue, or is busy with other events that occur before the timer, receipt
of the timer event can be very late. All that receiving a timer event does is tell
you that the time it measures has passed.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>An example of what this means is the display of a clock,
using the <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>extlib</span></span> time call. If we set a
recurrent timer to go off on every second, the program should NOT simply advance
the second on each timer event. Instead, the timer event should tell the
program to read time to determine if the second has changed, and what value it
currently has.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442710"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>E.11<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Mouse</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The mouse gives a position x,y on the screen, as well as
from 1 to 4 buttons on it. A mouse actually gives its position as relative
movements in x and y, but the system converts this to a screen position for
you. Its possible to have from 0 to 4 mice, and the function mouse returns the
number of mice attached to the system.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Mice generate two events. First, when the mouse moves, it
generates position changes via the <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etmoumov</span></span>
event. The program does not have to worry about where it is going. Each time
the position changes, a new x, y position is posted as an event.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The second event generated by a mouse is mouse button
asserts and deasserts, <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etmouba</span></span> and <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etmoubd</span></span>. An &quot;assert&quot;
means a press of the button, and a &quot;deassert&quot; is the release of the
button. Note that instead of an on/off status check as polled by the program, the
assert and deassert events give exact notice of when the button changes state,
and what it is changing to.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>When there is more than one mouse per system, the default
behavior should be to treat them as separate, but equal controls on the screen
from the same user. When a mouse moves or changes button state, it gets control
of the program. This matches the common use of multiple pointing devices, where
two devices are alternated by one user. For example, a trackball and a mouse
may be just two different input methods from one user.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Alternately, a second mouse can actually be a remote mouse
over a network. This &quot;collaborative computing&quot; model allows two users
to look at the same document, with separate mice.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442711"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>E.12<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Joysticks</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>From 0 to 4 joysticks may be supported. Each joystick can
have from 0 to 3 &quot;axes&quot; of directions of travel. In addition, each
joystick can have 0 to 4 buttons. The function joystick returns the number of
joysticks in the system. The function joyaxis gives the number of axes on a
given joystick. The function joybutton gives the number of buttons on a given
joystick.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The messages <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etjoyba</span></span>
or joystick button assert, and <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etjoybd</span></span>
or joystick button deassert, give events for the assertion and deassertion of
the buttons on a joystick. When any axis on a joystick moves, it generates a <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etjoymov</span></span>, or joystick movement,
event. This event gives the relative setting of each axis of the joystick.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Unlike a mouse, a joystick is entirely relative. Each axis
is represented by an integer. If the axis is not implemented it always reads 0.
If the axis is deflected left, up or in, depending on the type of axis, then it
is negative. If it is right, down, or out, it is positive. The axis is
determined in its amount of deflection. If it is in the middle, it is 0. If it
is deflected to the maximum, it is <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span>,
with the sign giving the direction.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>By convention, the axes on a joystick are:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo11'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>1.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Left/right, or slider.</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo11'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>2.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Up/down</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo11'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>3.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>In/out</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Joysticks are &quot;rate limited&quot; devices. This means
that no matter how fast the joystick is &quot;slewed&quot;, it will only
produce an event about every 10 milliseconds at maximum rate. The reason for
this is that humans cannot generally perceive events like movement of a pointer
across the screen at a faster rate than this, so there is no point in updating
faster than that, and flooding the input event queue.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442712"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>E.13<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Function
Keys</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The system may have from 0 to 100 function keys, which are
keys whose function are determined by the program. The number of function keys
implemented are found with funkey. Function key messages are sent by the
message etfun.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442713"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>E.14<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Terminal
objects</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>All of the procedures, functions and other declarations in <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>trmlib</span></span> are also available in a
terminal object. of the form:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'>Class terminal;</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'>var input, output: text; { input
and output files for this screen }</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>er: evtrec;<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>          </span>{ event record }</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'>{ procedures and functions from
trmlib }</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=Code0>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The complete catalog of procedures and functions from trmlib
are available as methods in the terminal class. There are minor differences,
which are detailed with the procedure and function descriptions in <!--[if supportFields]><span
style='mso-element:field-begin'></span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>REF _Ref251353925 \r \h <span
style='mso-element:field-separator'></span><![endif]-->E.16<!--[if gte mso 9]><xml>
 <w:data>08D0C9EA79F9BACE118C8200AA004BA90B02000000080000000E0000005F005200650066003200350031003300350033003900320035000000</w:data>
</xml><![endif]--><!--[if supportFields]><span style='mso-element:field-end'></span><![endif]-->.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>When a terminal object is instantiated, it’s input and
output files are automatically linked to the standard <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>input</span></span> and <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>output</span></span> files of the program.
Thus, where specifying the input and output files in <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>trmlib</span></span> procedures and functions
is optional, in methods of the terminal object these files <b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'><i style='mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>must not</i></b> be specified.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The input and output files used by the terminal object are
made available as class members input and output. This allows them to be used
in non-method procedures (such as read and write).</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>A terminal object also contains an event record, so it is
not necessary to specify an external event record in the <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>event</span></span> procedure.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>A terminal object can be created as follows:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>program p;<o:p></o:p></b></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></b></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>joins trmlib;<o:p></o:p></b></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></b></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>var</b> ti: instance of trmlib.terminal;</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'>begin</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>ti.home; { send cursor to home position }</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>writeln(ti.output, ‘hello, terminal world’);</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>repeat { event loop }</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>      </span>ti.event; { get next event }</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>      </span>{ process events }</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>until ti.event = etterm { loop until program cancelled }</p>

<p class=Code0 style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=Code0>end.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Where <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>terminal</span></span> is the
terminal object. Terminal objects can be instantiated statically or
dynamically.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Terminal objects contain their own state for the following:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo24'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>1.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Location of cursor.</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo24'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>2.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Current attributes and colors.</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo24'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>3.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Buffer working/display status.</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo24'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>4.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Tab stops.</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo24'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>5.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Timer numbers.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>However, each terminal object gets the complete state of the
module <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>trmlib</span></span> when it is created.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Having each terminal object possess its own state means that
each object can be writing to its own section of the screen in its own<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>mode. Each object can even have it’s own
private screen buffer, but this must be specifically selected using the <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>select</span></span> procedure.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>When multiple terminal objects exist, and all have the
cursor visibility on, the cursor will remain at the last place it was
specifically directed to. This can mean that the cursor will rapidly appear to
swap back and forth between the active drawing terminal objects. This can be
improved by only selecting one of the terminal objects as having a visible
cursor. Typically, a the cursor should be placed to attract user attention to
where text is being entered, or if none is being entered, it should be turned
off.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442714"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>E.15<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Exceptions</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The following exceptions are generated in <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>trmlib</span></span>:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>TooManyFIles<span style='mso-tab-count:3'>                         </span>The
total number of open files possible was exceeded.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>NoJoyStick<span style='mso-tab-count:3'>                              </span>No
joystick access was available.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>NoTimer<span style='mso-tab-count:3'>                                  </span>No
timer access was available.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>ToManyTimers<span style='mso-tab-count:3'>                                    </span>The
total number of timers available was exceeded.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>CannotPerformSpecial<span style='mso-tab-count:2'>             </span>Cannot
perform operation on specialfile.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>FilenameEmpty<span style='mso-tab-count:3'>                                    </span>Filename
specified was empty.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>InvalidScreenNumber<span style='mso-tab-count:2'>              </span>Screen
number specified was invalid.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>InvalidHandle<span style='mso-tab-count:3'>                          </span>An
invalid handle was specified.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>InvalidTab<span style='mso-tab-count:3'>                               </span>An
invalid tab position was specified.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>CannotCreateScreenBuffer<span style='mso-tab-count:1'>      </span>Cannot
create a buffer for the screen.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>CannotQueryJoystick<span style='mso-tab-count:2'>              </span>Could
not get information on joystick.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>InvalidJoystickHandle<span style='mso-tab-count:2'>             </span>Invalid
handle specified for joystick.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>InvalidTimerHandle<span style='mso-tab-count:2'>                 </span>Invalid
handle specified for timer.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>trmlib</span></span>
establishes a series of exception handlers for each of the above exceptions
during startup. Exceptions not handled by a client program of <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>trmlib</span></span> will go back to <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>trmlib</span></span>, then print a message
specific to the error, then the general exception will be thrown.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Not all procedures and functions throw all exceptions. See
each procedure or function description for a list of exceptions thrown. A
client of <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>trmlib</span></span> need only capture the
exceptions occurring in the procedure or function that is called.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442715"></a><a name="_Ref251353925"><span
style='mso-bookmark:_Toc251442715'><![if !supportLists]><span style='mso-fareast-font-family:
Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:none;text-underline:none'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>E.16<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Procedures, functions and methods in trmlib</span></a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>For all of the following calls, If the screen file <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> is not present, the default is
the standard input or output file. If the procedure or function is a method,
neither the input nor output screen file should be specified, since it is
inherent in the object.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure cursor([var f:
text;] x, y: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Set cursor
location for output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
in <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x</span></span> and <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function maxx[(var f: text)]:
integer;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Find
maximum screen location x in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function maxy[(var f: text)]:
integer;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Find
maximum screen location y in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure home[(var f: text)];</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Send
cursor to 1,1 location (upper left of screen) in output surface file <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><span lang=ES-CO
style='mso-ansi-language:ES-CO'>procedure del[(var f: text)];<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><span lang=ES-CO
style='mso-ansi-language:ES-CO'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Back up cursor
by one character in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>,
and erase character at that location. If the cursor is at the left side of the
screen, and automatic mode is on, the cursor will be moved up one line, and to
the right of screen. If the cursor is at the top of the screen, extreme left,
then the screen will be scrolled down one line, and the cursor moves to the
right side of the screen.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure up[(var f: text)];</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Move
cursor up one line in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.
If the cursor is already at the top line, and automatic mode is on, the screen
will be scrolled down, and the cursor remains at the same position.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure down[(var f: text)];</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Move cursor
down one line in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.
If the cursor is already at the bottom line, and automatic mode is on, the
screen will be scrolled up, and the cursor remains at the same position.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure left[(var f: text)];</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Back up cursor
by one character in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.
If the cursor is at the left side of the screen, and automatic mode is on, the
cursor will be moved up one line, and to the right of screen. If the cursor is
at the top of the screen, left, then the screen will be scrolled down one line,
and the cursor moves to the right side of the screen.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure right[(var f: text)];</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Move
forward by one character in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.
If the cursor is at the right side of the screen, and automatic mode is on, the
cursor will be moved down one line, and to the left of screen. If the cursor is
at the bottom of the screen, right, then the screen will be scrolled up one
line, and the cursor moves to the left side of the screen.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure blink([var f: text;]
e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span> is true, causes all further
characters written to the screen to appear in blinking text in output surface
file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure reverse([var f:
text;] e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span> is true, causes all further
characters written to the screen to appear in reverse text in output surface
file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure underline([var f:
text;] e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span> is true, causes all further
characters written to the screen to appear in underlined text in output surface
file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure superscript([var f:
text;] e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span> is true, causes all further characters
written to the screen to appear in superscript text in output surface file <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure subscript([var f:
text;] e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span> is true, causes all further
characters written to the screen to appear in subscript text in output surface
file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure italic([var f:
text;] e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span> is true, causes all further
characters written to the screen to appear in italic text in output surface
file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure bold([var f: text;]
e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span> is true, causes all further
characters written to the screen to appear in bold text in output surface file <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure strikeout([var f:
text;] e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>If <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span> is true, causes all further
characters written to the screen to appear in strikeout text in output surface
file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure standout([var f:
text;] e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>If <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span>
is true, causes all further characters written to the screen to appear in
standout text in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.
Standout is assigned to the first mode possible from the following order:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Reverse.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Underline.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Bold</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Italic.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Strikeout.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Blink.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>If none of those modes are
available, standout is a no-op.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure fcolor([var f:
text;] c: color);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Sets the
foreground, or text color, to the color <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>
in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure bcolor([var f:
text;] c: color);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Sets the
background, or space color, to the color <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>
in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure auto([var f: text;]
e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Turns
automatic mode on or off, according to <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span>
in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure curvis([var f:
text;] e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Turns
cursor visibility on or off, according to <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span>
in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure scroll([var f:
text;] x, y: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Scroll in arbitrary
directions. The screen is scrolled according to the differences in <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x</span></span> and <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y</span></span>.
Uncovered areas on the screen appear in the current background color.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function curx[(var f: text)]:
integer;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Find the
current x location of the cursor in output surface file <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function cury[(var f: text)]:
integer;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Find the
current y location of the cursor in output surface file <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function curbnd[(var f: text)]:
boolean;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Check cursor
in bounds. Returns true if the cursor is currently within the bounds of the
screen in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure select([var f:
text;] u, d: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Select
buffer to update and display. Selects the active buffer for update <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>u</span></span>, and display <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>d</span></span> in output surface file <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>. The update buffer will receive
the result of all writes. The display buffer will be shown on screen.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure event[([var f:
text;] var er: evtrec)];</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Get next
event. Retrieves the next event from the input queue from the terminal input
file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> to event record <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>er</span></span>. If there is no event ready,
the program will wait.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Note that specification
of the event record is optional only for the terminal class method.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure timer([var f: text;]
i: timhan; t: integer; r: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Set timer
active in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.
The timer <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>i</span></span> will be set to run for time <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>. If the repeat flag <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>r</span></span> is set, then the timer will
automatically repeat when the time expires. If the timer is already in use,
then it will cease its current timing, and perform the new time.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure killtimer([var f:
text;] i: timhan);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Stop timer
in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>. Stops the
timer <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>i</span></span>. If the timer is not active, no
error is reported.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function mouse[(var f: text)]:
mounum;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;page-break-after:avoid'>Returns the
number of mice in output surface file <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function mousebutton([var f:
text;] m: mouhan): moubut;</p>

