style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>H.14<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Procedures
and functions in widlib</span></span></a></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>For all of the following calls, If the screen file <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> is not present, the default is
the standard output file. If the procedure or function is a method, the output
screen file should not be specified, since it is inherent in the object.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure killwidget([var f:
text;] id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The widget within window <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
with the logical identifier <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span> is removed
from the system. It will be erased from the screen, and contents under it will
be restored as required.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure selectwidget([var
f: text; id: integer;] e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The widget within window <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
by the logical identifier <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span> will enter
the select state if <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span> is true,
otherwise the select state is removed. The exact effect of the select state
depends on the widget. See the individual widget to be selected for more
information. It is an error to select a widget that has no selectability.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>If the window file <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
does not exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>Selection
is typically used to indicate that the widget is &quot;on&quot;, by changing
its face appearance. For example, it can be checked, pressed or similar.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure enablewidget([var
f: text;] id: integer; e: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The widget within window <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
by the logical identifier <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span> will enter
the enable state if <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>e</span></span> is true,
otherwise the disable state is entered. The exact effect of the enable or
disable state depends on the widget. See the individual widget to be selected
for more information. It is an error to enable or disable a widget that has no
such capability. The default state for all widgets is to be enabled. A widget
that is disabled will stop sending events.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>If the window file <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
does not exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>Disabling
a widget is typically used to mark it as unusable or invalid in the current
context. An example would be a &quot;next&quot; button where no next page or
item exists. The standard method used to indicate disabled widgets is to give
them a &quot;greyed out&quot; appearance, but the actual effect may depend on
the operating system.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure getwidgettext([var
f: text;] id: integer; var s: pstring);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Retrives the text contained by the widget with the
logical identifier <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span> within
window <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, and returns the text as a
dynamic string <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>. It depends
on the widget as to if it has text that can be read. It is an error to get text
from a widget that has no such capability.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>If the window file <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
does not exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>Widgets
can typically have their text read if the widget provides the user with the ability
to modify or edit text. In this case, retrieving the text is required to obtain
the new text.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure putwidgettext([var
f: text;] id: integer; view s: string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Places text in the widget with the logical identifier <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span> within window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> from the string <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>. It depends on the widget as to
if it can accept text placed in this manner. It is an error to place text in a
widget that has no such capability.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>If the window file <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
does not exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>A
widget will have the ability to place text if it can edit text by the user.
Placing text in the widget can be used to initalize the contents of such a
widget, or as part of the overall interaction with the user.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>procedure sizwidget[g]([var f: text;] id: integer; x, y: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Resize an existing widget. The
widget with the logical identifier <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>
is resized to be the size in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x</span></span> and <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y</span></span>, in the window f.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>If the graphical version is used,
the size is in pixels, otherwise, the size is in characters.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>If the window file <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
does not exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>procedure poswidget[g]([var f: text;] id: integer; x, y:
integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Reposition an existing widget.
The widget with the logical identifier <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>
is repositioned to be at the position <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x</span></span>
and <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y</span></span>, in the parent window of the
window f.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>If the graphical version is used,
the size is in pixels, otherwise, the size is in characters.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>If the window file <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
does not exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure buttonsiz[g]([var
f: text;] view s: string; var w, h: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the minimum size of a button within window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with face text string <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>. The width to use is returned
in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, and the height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. Button sizing returns the
minimum size in terms of the minimum amount of space needed to contain the face
text, in the labeling font, and the border of the button itself. You will want
to use the size as a guide to button sizing, and not for the actual size of the
button. A good rule of thumb is to add %25 of the minimum height of the button
to the actual height and width of the button to give the user sufficient area
to click on the button. In addition, buttons should be &quot;justified&quot;
when they appear in groups to appear as the same width. This is done by
calculating a maximum size for a group of related buttons, then using the same
width and height for all of them.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure button[g]([var f:
text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; view s: string; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Places a button within window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> in the bounding box formed by <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
with the face text from the string <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>.
The logical identifier is specified in <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>,
which must be an integer from 1 to n, which is not currently in use in any
other widget. The button drawn is not garanteed to completely fill the bounding
box. The button should be placed against a background that is colored with the
standard background color. The button will be placed at the front of the window
stacking order, and should be placed after any other widgets or child windows
that the button is to appear in front of.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>When the button is pressed, it will send an <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etbutton</span></span> event, which contains
the logical id of the button that was pressed. It is up to the system whether
the event occurs when the button is depressed or released.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>Buttons
cannot be selected, or have their face text changed or read. Buttons can be
enabled and disabled. If the button is disabled, it will not sent <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etbutton</span></span> events when pressed.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure checkboxsiz[g]([var
f: text;] view s: string; var w, h: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the minimum size of a checkbox within window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with face text string <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>. The width to use is returned
in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, and the height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. Checkbox sizing returns the
minimum size in terms of the minimum amount of space needed to contain the face
text, in the labeling font, and the border of the checkbox itself, if it
exists. You will want to use the size as a guide to checkbox sizing, and not
for the actual size of the checkbox. A good rule of thumb is to add %25 of the
minimum height of the checkbox to the actual height and width of the checkbox
to give the user sufficient area to click on the checkbox.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure checkbox[g]([var f:
text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; view s: string; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Places a checkbox within window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> in the bounding box formed by <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
with the face text from the string <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>.
The logical identifier is specified in <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>,
which must be an integer from 1 to n, which is not currently in use in any
other widget. The checkbox drawn is not garanteed to completely fill the
bounding box. The checkbox should be placed against a background that is
colored with the standard background color. The checkbox will be placed at the
front of the window stacking order, and should be placed after any other
widgets or child windows that the checkbox is to appear in front of.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>If the window file <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
does not exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>When the checkbox is clicked, it will send an <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etchkbox</span></span> event, which contains
the logical id of the checkbox that was pressed. It is up to the system whether
the event occurs when the checkbox is depressed or released.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Checkboxes cannot have their face text changed or read.
A checkbox can be selected or deselected, and can be enabled and disabled. If
the checkbox is selected, it will appear with a selected face, which is
typically a checkmark in a box. If the checkbox is disabled, it will not sent
etchkbox events when pressed.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>A
checkbox only changes its appearance in response to a select, and does not keep
a state that can be read by the program. Its up to the program to keep track of
the state of the checkbox, and how to handle it. In particular, if the checkbox
is pressed, it is up to the program to change its select status, otherwise the
press will have no effect. The program can implement many different effects for
checkboxes. The checkbox can toggle, or it can be one of a series of mutually
exclusive selections.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure radiobuttonsiz[g]([var
f: text;] view s: string; var w, h: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the minimum size of a radio button within window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with face text string <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>. The width to use is returned
in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, and the height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. Radio button sizing returns
the minimum size in terms of the minimum amount of space needed to contain the
face text, in the labeling font, and the border of the radio button, if it
exists. You will want to use the size as a guide to radio button sizing, and
not for the actual size of the checkbox. A good rule of thumb is to add %25 of
the minimum height of the radio button to the actual height and width of the
radio button to give the user sufficient area to click on the radio button.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file f does not exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by
default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure radiobutton[g]([var
f: text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; view s: string; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Places a radio button within window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> in the bounding box formed by <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
with the face text from the string <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>.
The logical identifier is specified in <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>,
which must be an integer from 1 to n, which is not currently in use in any
other widget. The radio button drawn is not garanteed to completely fill the
bounding box. The radio button should be placed against a background that is
colored with the standard background color. The radio button will be placed at
the front of the window stacking order, and should be placed after any other
widgets or child windows that the radio button is to appear in front of.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>If the window file <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
does not exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>When the radio button is pressed, it will send an <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etradbut</span></span> event, which contains
the logical id of the radio button that was pressed. It is up to the system
whether the event occurs when the radio button is depressed or released.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Radio buttons cannot have their face text changed or
read. A radio button can be selected or deselected, and can be enabled and
disabled. If the radio button is selected, it will appear with a selected face,
which is typically a blacked out radio button. If the radio button is disabled,
it will not sent <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etradbut</span></span> events
when pressed.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>A
radio button only changes its appearance in response to a select, and does not
keep a state that can be read by the program. Its up to the program to keep
track of the state of the radio button, and how to handle it. In particular, if
the checkbox is pressed, it is up to the program to change its select status,
otherwise the press will have no effect. The program can implement many
different effects for radio buttons. The radio button can toggle, or it can be
one of a series of mutually exclusive selections.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure groupsiz[g]([var f:
text;] view s: string; cw, ch: integer; var w, h, ox, oy: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the required size of a group box in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with the face text given in
string <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>, and the client area width <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>cw</span></span>, and client area height <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>ch</span></span>. The required width is
returned in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, the height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>, and the offset to the client
area in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x</span></span> and <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y</span></span>.
A group box consists of a border area, a label, and an internal client area.
Group boxes are designed to be layered components. They contain other widgets,
and provide a background for them. When a group size is found, the minimum size
is found as what will contain all of the border, face text and the requested client
area. The program will know where to place its widgets in the client area by
the client offset, which is given as a difference between the bounding box
origin, and the origin of the client rectangle.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure group[g]([var f:
text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; view s: string; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a group box in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> within the bounding rectangle <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
the face text given in string <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>, and with the
logical identifier <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>. Group boxes
are containers for other widgets, and consist of a border area, the face text,
and an internal client area where other widgets are to be placed.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The entire client area of the group will have the
standard background color, and widgets can be placed into the client in any
arrangement or number. The program should be sure to create the client area
widgets after the group is created, so that they will appear in front of the group
in stacking order.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The location of the client area within a group box can
be found with the group sizing call.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure background[g]([var
f: text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a background box in the window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with the bounding rectangle <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
and the logical widget identifier <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>.
A background is simply a rectangle with the standard background color. It is
more convienent than simply painting a rectangle on the window with the
background color because it handles its own redraws. Because a background box
has no borders, widgets can be placed within it anywhere, and in any number.
Any widgets to be placed within the group should be created after the group box
is created, so that that they are on top of the group box in stacking order.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure scrollvertsiz[g]([var
f: text;] var w, h: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the size for a vertical scroll bar in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>. Returns the width in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, and the height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. Scrollbars typically can be
sized to any size, and the width of a vertical scroll bar is a suggested width
designed to match others used in the same system. The height of a vertical
scrollbar is simply a suggestion, and can be ignored.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>If a scrollbar cannot be arbitrarily sized, then the
width and height will reflect the demensions of a fixed scrollbar.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure scrollvert[g]([var
f: text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a vertical scrollbar in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with bounding rectange <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
and logical widget identifier <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>. If
possible, the scrollbar is made to fill the width and height requested. If this
is not possible, then the largest scrollbar is created that fits within the
bounding rectangle. There is no garantee that the scrollbar will completely
fill the rectangle. The area under the scrollbar should be drawn with the standard
background color.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The scrollbar will generate several events when
clicked. The <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etsclull</span></span> event indicates the line
up button of the scrollbar was pressed. The <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etscldrl</span></span>
event indicates the line down button of the scrollbar was pressed. The <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etsclulp</span></span> event indicates the page
up section of the scrollbar was pressed. The <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etscldrp</span></span>
event indicates the page down section of the scrollbar was pressed. It is
system dependent as to whether the buttons generate their events on a button
press or a button release.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etsclpos</span></span> event
gives the position of the top of the slider after the user moves it. The
positition is returned as a ratioed <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span>
number, where 0 means the slider is at the top, and <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span>
means the slider is at the bottom. The number is affected by the size of the
slider. If, for example, the slider occupies %50 of the scrollbar, then only
the positions 0 to <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span> <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>div</span></span> 2 will be generated. It is
undefined as to exactly when etsclpos events occur. They may only be generated
when the slider is moved and then released, or they may be generated
continuously as the slider is moved. If the generation is continuous, then the
movements are usually subject to &quot;rate limiting&quot; to keep them from
generating events too fast to handle.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The scrollbar will not change position on its own. The
scrollbar will generate events, and it is up to the program to use those to set
the scrollbar slider position, and to take action on them, such as move the
screen data up or down. The page up/down and line up/down terminology is suggestive
of the use of these events, but it is up to the program exactly how to use or
implement these functions. Typically, these are used to move the displayed area
of a document one line up or down, and one page or screenful up or down.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The size of the scrollbar slider is set by default to
small, but convienent for the user to press and manipulate. This can be left
alone for programs that don't require sized scrollbar sliders. The size of the
slider is set by <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>scrollsiz[g]</span></span>.
Typically, it is used to set the ratio of onscreen data shown to the entire
document or other data avialable. For example, if %50 of the document is being
displayed, then the slider should occupy %50 of the scrollbar.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure scrollhorizsiz[g]([var
f: text;] var w, h: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the size for a horizontal scroll bar in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>. Returns the width in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, and the height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. Scrollbars typically can be
sized to any size, and the height of a horizontal scroll bar is a suggested
width designed to match others used in the same system. The width of a
horizontal scrollbar is simply a suggestion, and can be ignored.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>If a scrollbar cannot be arbitrarily sized, then the
width and height will reflect the demensions of a fixed scrollbar.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure scrollhoriz[g]([var
f: text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a horizontal scrollbar in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with bounding rectange <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
and logical widget identifier <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>. If
possible, the scrollbar is made to fill the width and height requested. If this
is not possible, then the largest scrollbar is created that fits within the
bounding rectangle. There is no garantee that the scrollbar will completely
fill the rectangle. The area under the scrollbar should be drawn with the
standard background color.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The scrollbar will generate several events when
clicked. The <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etsclull</span></span> event indicates the line
left button of the scrollbar was pressed. The <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etscldrl</span></span>
event indicates the line right button of the scrollbar was pressed. The <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etsclulp</span></span> event indicates the page
left section of the scrollbar was pressed. The <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etscldrp</span></span>
event indicates the page right section of the scrollbar was pressed. It is
system dependent as to whether the buttons generate their events on a button
press or a button release.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etsclpos</span></span> event
gives the position of the left of the slider after the user moves it. The
positition is returned as a ratioed <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span>
number, where 0 means the slider is at the left, and <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span>
means the slider is at the right. The number is affected by the size of the
slider. If, for example, the slider occupies %50 of the scrollbar, then only
the positions 0 to <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span> <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>div</span></span> 2 will be generated. It is
undefined as to exactly when etsclpos events occur. They may only be generated
when the slider is moved and then released, or they may be generated
continuously as the slider is moved. If the generation is continuous, then the
movements are usually subject to &quot;rate limiting&quot; to keep them from
generating events too fast to handle.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The scrollbar will not change position on its own. The
scrollbar will generate events, and it is up to the program to use those to set
the scrollbar slider position, and to take action on them, such as move the
screen data left or right. The page left/right and line left/right terminology
is suggestive of the use of these events, but it is up to the program exactly
how to use or implement these functions. Typically, these are used to move the
displayed area of a document one character left or right, and one page or
screenful left or right.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The size of the scrollbar slider is set by default to
small, but convienent for the user to press and manipulate. This can be left
alone for programs that don't require sized scrollbar sliders. The size of the
slider is set by <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>scrollsiz[g]</span></span>.
Typically, it is used to set the ratio of onscreen data shown to the entire
document or other data avialable. For example, if %50 of the document is being
displayed, then the slider should occupy %50 of the scrollbar.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure scrollpos([var f:
text;] id: integer; p: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Sets the scrollbar slider position for window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, scrollbar identifier <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>, to position <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>. The position is in ratioed <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span> format. That is, 0 means
to set the position to the top or left, and maxint means bottom or right. The
position is affected by the size of the scrollbar slider. For example, if the
slider occupies %50 of the scrollbar, then the range of positions would only be
from 0 to maxint div 2. If the position given is beyond the maximum position
possible, then the slider is set to<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>the
maximum travel position, and no error occurs. It is an error if the position is
negative.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The program must specifically set the position of the
scrollbar. The user moving the scrollbar slider may temporarily move the slider
while it is being moved, but this will not remain in position after the user
releases it. The program must specifically set the scrollbar position in
response to the event.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure scrollsiz([var f:
text;] id: integer; s: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Sets the size of the scrollbar slider in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, logical identifer <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>, to the size <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>. The size of the scrollbar
slider is a <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span> ratio, with 0 meaning
infinitely small, and <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span> meaning
that it occupies the entire scrollbar. In practice, there is a practical limit
to how small the slider can be. If the slider is set too small, it will be set
to the minimum size, and no error will occur. If the size set is negative, then
an error will result.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>If the window file <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>
does not exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The size of the scrollbar is set to a reasonable
default if it is never specifically set. This is typically a fairly small size that
is still easy to press and manipulate by the user.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>This allows the scrollbar to be used when
slider sizing is not supported by the program.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The meaning of the scrollbar slider size is up to the
program. However, it is typically used to indicate how much of the data is
onscreen. For example, if a document has %50 of its content currently
displayed, then the slider would be set to %50 of the scrollbar.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure numselboxsiz[g]([var
f: text;] l, u: integer; var w, h: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the width and height of a number select box for
window <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with lower number limit <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>l</span></span> and upper number limit <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>u</span></span>. The width required is returned
in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, and the height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. The minimum width and height
is determined by the maximum length of the number to be displayed, with borders
and up/down arrows considered. This can be used without adding extra space.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><span lang=ES-CO
style='mso-ansi-language:ES-CO'>procedure numselbox[g]([var f: text;] x1, y1,
x2, y2: integer; l, u: integer; id: integer);<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><span lang=ES-CO
style='mso-ansi-language:ES-CO'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a number select box for window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, in the rectangle <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
with lower number limit <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>l</span></span>, and upper
number limit <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>u</span></span>. The default number appearing
in the box is set to the lower limit. The number select box allows the user to
edit the number, or use up/down arrow controls to select the number. Any digits
typed into the edit section are limited to the digits 0-9, and negative numbers
are not allowed. When the user presses enter to the number edit box, an event, <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etnumbox</span></span> will be sent, which
includes the number selected.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure editboxsiz[g]([var
f: text;] view s: string; var w, h: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the size of an edit box for window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with face text string <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>. The width is returned in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, and the height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. The string passed is a dummy,
and will not be used for any purpose other than as a reference to determine the
width of the required edit box. The string should contain text that is
representative of the string to be editted. This could be the string that you
plan to place in the edit box as its default, or it could be the worst case
contents of the edit box. For example, if 8 characters is the planned edit
width, the string &quot;WWWWWWWW&quot; (8 &quot;W&quot; characters) would be
the largest width of edit possible. The edit box is sized to be the minimum
appropriate, and can be used without extra added space.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure editbox[g]([var f:
text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates an edit box for window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, in rectangle <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
with logical identifier <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>. Edit boxes
can be used to allow the user to enter any text. The text within an edit box
can be set by <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>putwidgettext</span></span>, and retrieved by <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>getwidgettext</span></span>. This can occur at
any time. When the user presses enter in the edit box, it sends an <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etedtbox</span></span> event. The program can
then retrieve the text from the edit box.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure progbarsiz[g]([var
f: text;] var w, h: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the size of a progress bar for window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>. The width is returned in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, and the height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. For systems that can size
progress bars arbitrarily, the height is returned as the size that matches
others used in the system. The width is a suggestion, and can be ignored.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure progbar[g]([var f:
text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a progress bar in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, in rectangle <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
with logical identifier <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>. The
progress bar starts by default at 0, and is entirely operated by the program
with <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>progbarpos</span></span> calls.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure progbarpos([var f:
text;] id: integer; pos: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Sets the progress bar in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with logical identifier <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>, to the position <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>pos</span></span>. The position is a ratioed <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span> number, from 0 to <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span>. 0 indicates &quot;no
progress&quot;, and maxint indicates &quot;complete&quot;. Because of rounding,
it is recommended that the program specifically set maxint at completion,
instead of using a formula.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure listboxsiz[g]([var
f: text;] sp: strptr; var w, h: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the required size of a listbox for window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with string list <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sp</span></span>. The required width is
returned in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, and the required height is
returned in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. A listbox is sized such that
all of the strings in the string list can be presented in it, with borders
added. No extra space is required.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure listbox[g]([var f:
text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; sp: strptr; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a listbox for window <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>,
in rectangle <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
with string list <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sp</span></span>, and logical
identifier <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>. A listbox contains a series
of strings that can be selected by the user. When the user clicks a string, the
event <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etlstbox</span></span> will be sent, which
contains the number of the selected string in list order. For example, the
first string in the list would be 1, and second string in the list 2, etc. If
there is not enough room in the height of the listbox for all strings in the
list to be presented, then the widget will use a compression method to fit the
available space. This is typically done by allowing the user to scroll through
the selections. If there is not enough width for the strings in the list, they
are typically clipped at the right.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure dropboxsiz[g](var
f: text; sp: strptr; var cw, ch, ow, oh: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the size of a drop box for window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with string list sp. The
closed width is returned in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>cw</span></span>, and the
closed height in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. The open
width is returned in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>ow</span></span>, and the
height in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>oh</span></span>. Drop boxes are used to
display a list of selections as in a listbox, but they occupy less space than a
listbox. Dropboxes have two bounding rectangles, one is its demensions when
closed, and another when the user drops it down, or opens it. Both sizes are
returned. This allows layout planning for both modes of the widget. Generally,
the closed size is used to plan placement, then the open size is used to check
if the widget will extend past the edges of the window when open.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure dropbox[g]([var f:
text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; sp: strptr; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a dropbox in the window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, within rectangle <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
for string list <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sp</span></span>, with
logical identifier <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>. The
bounding rectangle for a drop box specifies its open mode, where the user has
selected and dropped down the list of items. If the size specified is greater
than or equal to the open size, as determined by <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>dropboxsiz</span></span>,
then the entire dropbox will be presented. If the size is between the closed
size and the open size, the system will attempt to work around the fact that
the entire list cannot be dropped down. This is typically done by allowing the
user to scroll though the list. If the size is less than the closed size, the
dropbox will be clipped.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>When a string within the drop box is selected, it will
send an <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etdrpbox</span></span> event. It contains the
sequential number of the string that was selected. For example, the first
string sends 1, the second in the list sends 2, etc.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure dropeditboxsiz[g]([var
f: text;] sp: strptr; var cw, ch, ow, oh: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the size of a drop edit box for window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with string list sp. The
closed width is returned in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>cw</span></span>, and the
closed height in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. The open
width is returned in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>ow</span></span>, and the
height in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>oh</span></span>. Drop edit boxes boxes are
used to display a list of selections, and acts as a combination of a list and
edit box, but they occupy less space than a listbox. Drop edit boxes have two
bounding rectangles, one is its demensions when closed, and another when the
user drops it down, or opens it. Both sizes are returned. This allows layout
planning for both modes of the widget. Generally, the closed size is used to
plan placement, then the open size is used to check if the widget will extend
past the edges of the window when open.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure dropeditbox[g]([var
f: text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; sp: strptr; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a drop edit box in the window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, within rectangle <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
for string list <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sp</span></span>, with
logical identifier <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>. The
bounding rectangle for a drop edit box specifies its open mode, where the user
has selected and dropped down the list of items. If the size specified is
greater than or equal to the open size, as determined by <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>dropboxsiz</span></span>, then the entire
dropbox will be presented. If the size is between the closed size and the open
size, the system will attempt to work around the fact that the entire list
cannot be dropped down. This is typically done by allowing the user to scroll
though the list. If the size is less than the closed size, the dropbox will be
clipped.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>When a drop box string is selected, or enter is hit
while editing, it sends the event <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etdrebox</span></span>.
There is no other information associated with this event. Since the text is
editable, it could be anything, and may not match one of the list entries.
Instead, the program should use <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>getwidgettext</span></span>
to retrieve the result of the edit.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Drop edit boxes default to a blank edit string. The
idea of the drop edit box is that the user can simply use it as an edit box to
enter the needed data, or drop down a list of preselected items. If you wish to
make one of the string list items the default, or even a text that is not on
the list, use the <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>putwidgettext</span></span>
to initalize the edit field.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure slidehorizsiz[g]([var
f: text;] var w, h: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the size of a horizontal scrollbar for window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>. The required width is returned
in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, and the required height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. The height of a slider is
choosen so that they match other slidebars used in the system. The width is a
suggestion, and can be ignored.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure slidehoriz[g]([var
f: text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; mark: integer; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a horizontal slider in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, in bounding rectangle <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
with <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>mark</span></span> number of tick marks, and a
logical identifer <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>. Sliders
give a convenient way to select from a range of values. The system will either
size the slider to fit the given rectangle, or choose the slider representation
that is as large as possible, but still fits the given rectangle. It is not
garanteed that the slider will fill the entire rectangle. This means that it is
important for the entire background under the regtangle to be set to the standard
background color.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>When the slider is moved by the user, it generates a <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etsldpos</span></span> event. This event
carries the new position of the slider, which is a ratioed <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span> number, from 0 to <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span>. 0 means the slider is at
the extreme left, and <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span> means
the slider is at the extreme right.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>There is no garantee as to when a slider generates its
events. It can generate them as the slider is moved, or it may wait until the
user moves, and then releases the slider to generate events. Sliders automatically
update the position of the slider, and do not need to be set by the program.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The number of tick marks given by <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>mark</span></span> are evenly distributed
across the slider. If <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>mark</span></span> is zero,
then no tick marks are placed at all. Tick marks have no other effect besides
appearing on the slider.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure slidevertsiz[g]([var
f: text;] var w, h: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the size of a vertical slider for window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>. The required width is returned
in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, and the required height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>. The width of a slider is
choosen so that they match other slidebars used in the system. The height is a
suggestion, and can be ignored.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure slidevert[g]([var
f: text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; mark: integer; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a vertical slider in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, in bounding rectangle <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x1</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y1</span></span>,
<span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>x2</span></span>, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>y2</span></span>,
with mark number of tick marks, and a logical identifer <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>id</span></span>. Sliders give a convenient way
to select from a range of values. The system will either size the slider to fit
the given rectangle, or choose the slider representatin that is as large as
possible, but still fits the given rectangle. It is not garanteed that the
slider will fill the entire rectangle. This means that it is important for the
entire background under the regtangle to be set to the standard background
color.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>When the slider is moved by the user, it generates a <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>etsldpos</span></span> event. This event
carries the new position of the slider, which is a ratioed <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span> number, from 0 to <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span>. 0 means the slider is at
the extreme top, and maxint means the slider is at the extreme bottom.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>There is no garantee as to when a slider generates its
events. It can generate them as the slider is moved, or it may wait until the
user moves, and then releases the slider to generate events. Sliders
automatically update the position of the slider, and do not need to be set by
the program.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The number of tick marks given by <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>mark</span></span> are evenly distributed
across the slider. If <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>mark</span></span> is zero,
then no tick marks are placed at all. Tick marks have no other effect besides
appearing on the slider.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure tabbarsiz[g[([var
f: text;] tat, tar, tab, tal: boolean; cw, ch: integer; var w, h, ox, oy:
integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the size of a tabbar, in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with tab side active state <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tat</span></b>,
<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tar</span></b>,
<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tab</span></b>,
<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tal</span></b>,
client width <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>cw</span></span>, and client height <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>ch</span></span>. The required width is
returned in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, the height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>, and the client offset in x and
y. The size of a tabbar is enough to hold the height of the labeling font (in
whatever orientation), plus border areas, any selection scrolling arrows, and
the client area.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>A tabbar can have tabs on any of its four sides. The enables
for the tabs on a side are:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:72.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tat</span></b><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>        </span>Top</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:72.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tar</span></b><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>       </span>Right</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:72.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tab</span></b><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>       </span>Bottom</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:72.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tal</span></b><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>        </span>Left</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>They are in clockwise order starting from the top.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:106.35pt;text-indent:-106.35pt;
page-break-after:avoid'>procedure tabbarclient[g[([var f: text;] tat, tar, tab,
tal: boolean; w, h: integer; var cw, ch, ox, oy: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Finds the size of a tabbar client area, in window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with tab side active state <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tat</span></b>,
<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tar</span></b>,
<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tab</span></b>,
<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tal</span></b>,
tabbar width <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>cw</span></span>, and tab bar height <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>ch</span></span>. The client width is returned
in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>w</span></span>, the height in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>h</span></span>, and the client offset in x and
y. This procedure is used to find the client area for a specific size of
tabbar.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>A tabbar can have tabs on any of its four sides. The
enables for the tabs on a side are:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:72.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tat</span></b><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>        </span>Top</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:72.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tar</span></b><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>       </span>Right</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:72.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tab</span></b><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>       </span>Bottom</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:72.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>tal</span></b><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>        </span>Left</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>They are in clockwise order starting from the top.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure tabbar[g]([var f:
text;] x1, y1, x2, y2: integer; spt, spr, spb, spl: strptr; id: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a tab bar, in the window <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span>, with string lists <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>spt, spr, spb, spl</span></span>, and logical
identifier id. A tabbar gives the user a paradygm of a book with tabs on the
side. The list of tabs, which are specified by the program, each generate
events. The program establishes the view to be selected in the client area at
the center of the tabbar, then it uses the tab events to switch the views in
the client. If there is not enough area to display the full list of tabs, the
system will allow the user to scroll through them with arrows.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>To locate the tabbar and client, the <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>tabbarsiz</span></span> call is used to
establish the size and client offset. Then, the client is offset into the
tabbar. The client widgets or child windows must be created after the tabbar in
order to be placed to the front of the stacking order.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>When a tab is selected, it generates an <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>ettabbar</span></span> event, which contains
both the logical tabbar id, and the number of the string list that was
selected. This number will be the number in the string list. For example, the
first string in the list will be 1, the second 2, etc.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>A tabbar can have tabs on any of its four sides. The
string lists that form the tabs on a side are:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:72.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>spt</span></b><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>       </span>Top</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:72.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>spr</span></b><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>      </span>Right</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:72.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>spb</span></b><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>      </span>Bottom</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:72.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>spl</span></b><span style='mso-tab-count:
1'>       </span>Left</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>They are in clockwise order starting from the top.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>If tabs are not required on a given side, the string
list for that side is passed as nil. When a tab list is not active on a side,
the client area will be extended to cover the tabs on that side. If no tab
string list is active, then a tabbar is equivalent to a group.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the window file <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>f</span></span> does not
exist, the &quot;output&quot; file will be used by default.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure alert(view title,
msg: string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>Creates
an alert dialog, with window title <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>title</span></span>,
and client message <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>msg</span></span>. The alert
dialog is a freestanding window that is placed at the front of the desktop
stacking order. It is generally used to display an error, warning or other
attention condition. The window title should tell the user what application is
generating the alert, and the client message should give the error or warning.
The user dismisses the dialog, and the program holds until the dialog
completes.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure querycolor(var r,
g, b: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>Creates
a color select dialog. The dialog &quot;flows through&quot; to set its
parameters. When called, <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>r</span></span> contains the
default red, <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>g</span></span> the default green, and <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>b</span></span> the default blue colors. These
defaults are used to set the dialog default selection. When the user chooses a
color, the same parameters return the new selection. If the user cancels, or
leaves the default selection alone, the input colors will simply be left as the
default output colors. The dialog is presented to the front of the desktop
stacking order, and the program holds until the dialog is complete.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure queryopen(var s:
pstring);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates an open file dialog. The dialog &quot;flows
through&quot; to set its parameters. When called, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>
contains a default filename to open (which could be null). This default is used
to initalize the dialog default. When the user edits a filename, that is then
returned in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> as well. The input and out put
strings are not the same even if the user chooses the default. The result
string must be disposed of by the caller, and the default string supplied to
the dialog is allocated and deallocated entirely by the caller as well. The
dialog is presented to the front of the desktop stacking order, and the program
holds until the dialog is complete.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the user cancels, a null string is returned (a string with zero length, not a
nil pointer).</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure querysave(var s:
pstring);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates an save file dialog. The dialog &quot;flows
through&quot; to set its parameters. When called, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>
contains a default filename to save (which could be null). This default is used
to initalize the dialog default. When the user edits a filename, that is then
returned in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> as well. The input and out put
strings are not the same even if the user chooses the default. The result
string must be disposed of by the caller, and the default string supplied to
the dialog is allocated and deallocated entirely by the caller as well. The
dialog is presented to the front of the desktop stacking order, and the program
holds until the dialog is complete.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the user cancels, a null string is returned (a string with zero length, not a
nil pointer).</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure queryfind(var s:
pstring; var opt: qfnopts);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a find string dialog. The dialog &quot;flows
through&quot; to set its parameters. When called, <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span>
contains a default search string (which could be null). This default is used to
initalize the dialog default. When the user edits a search, that is then
returned in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> as well. The input and out put
strings are not the same even if the user chooses the default. The result
string must be disposed of by the caller, and the default string supplied to
the dialog is allocated and deallocated entirely by the caller as well. The
dialog is presented to the front of the desktop stacking order, and the program
holds until the dialog is complete.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The find dialog may set one or more of several options
from the set provided in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>opt</span></span>. These are
set before the call, and they are used to initalize the defaults in the dialog.
When the dialog terminates, the new state of the options are returned in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>opt</span></span> as well. If the dialog does
not implement a particular option, then the input value will simply be copied
to the output value without change.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'>If
the user cancels, a null string is returned (a string with zero length, not a
nil pointer).</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure queryfindrep(var s,
r: pstring; var opt: qfropts);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

