page-break-after:avoid'>Creates a find/replace string dialog. The dialog
&quot;flows through&quot; to set its parameters. When called, <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> contains a default search
string (which could be null), and <span class=referenceChar><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>r</span></span>
contains the default replacement string (which could be null). This default is
used to initalize the dialog default. When the user edits a search, that is
then returned in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>s</span></span> and <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>r</span></span> as well. The input and out put
strings are not the same even if the user chooses the default. The result
strings must be disposed of by the caller, and the default strings supplied to
the dialog are allocated and deallocated entirely by the caller as well. The dialog
is presented to the front of the desktop stacking order, and the program holds
until the dialog is complete.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'>The find dialog may set one or more of several options
from the set provided in <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>opt</span></span>. These are
set before the call, and they are used to initalize the defaults in the dialog.
When the dialog terminates, the new state of the options are returned in <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>opt</span></span> as well. If the dialog does
not implement a particular option, then the input value will simply be copied
