</span>

<div class=Section12>

<p class=MsoHeading7><a name="_Toc251442772"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>I<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Annex I: Sound Library</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sndlib</span></span> adds
both a synthesizer interface via the MIDI standard, and the ability to play
wave files. It implements or takes advantage of a sequencer that programs the
exact time at which each of the events to make a complex combination of sounds
occur.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The MIDI interface is defined as a serial interface, but the
target of a MIDI port can be a standard serial MIDI daisy chain, another type
of interface that carries MIDI commands (such as USB), or simply terminate in
an internal sound card or even a software sythesiser.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442773"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>I.1<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Ports</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>A port is the basic MIDI output device. Typically, a
computer has two of them, the sound card internal to the computer, and the
external MIDI jack. These ports are labeled <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>synth_out</span></span>
and <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>synth_ext</span></span>, respectively. A synthesizer
output is opened with <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>opensynthout</span></span>.
It can be closed with <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>closesynthout</span></span>.
All synthesizer ports are automatically closed when the program closes.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code>synth_out = 1; { the default output synth for host }</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code>synth_ext = 2; { the default output to external synth }</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The total number of synthesizer output ports is found by
synthout. Notes</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>type</b> note = 1..128; {
note number for midi }</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The basic work of making music is playing notes. MIDI can
play 128 notes, numbered from 1 to 128. This ranges in frequency from 8 Hertz,
or cycles per second, to 12 Kilohertz. This is approximately the range of human
hearing. MIDI can also change each note in frequency enough to move it to the
note next to it (and then some), so MIDI is able to reach any frequency
desired.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Humans perceive a frequency that is 4 times higher as being
only twice as high. If a musical note is doubled in frequency, it will be perceived
as the same note one octave higher. There are twelve notes in an octave. In the
lowest octave, they are:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>{ the notes in the lowest octave }</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_c<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>   </span>= 1;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_c_sharp<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 2;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_d_flat<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>   </span>= 2;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_d<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>        </span>= 3;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_d_sharp<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 4;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_e_flat<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>= 4;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_e<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>        </span>= 5;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_f<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>      </span>= 6;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_f_sharp <span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>= 7;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_g_flat<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>= 7;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_g<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>        </span>= 8;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_g_sharp<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 9;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_a_flat<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>   </span>= 9;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_a<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>        </span>= 10;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_a_sharp <span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>= 11;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>note_b_flat <span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>= 11;</p>

<p class=code>note_b<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>      </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>= 12;</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The bases of the octaves are:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>{ the octaves of midi, add to note
to place in that octave }</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>octave_1<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 0;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>octave_2<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 12;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>octave_3<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 24;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>octave_4<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 36;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>octave_5<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 48;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>octave_6<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 60;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>octave_7<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 72;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>octave_8<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 84;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>octave_9<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 96;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>octave_10 = 108;</p>

<p class=code>octave_11 = 120;</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>So any note in any octave can be found by:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>note+octave</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>For example, C in the 6th Octave:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>note_c+octave_6</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Notes are activated in MIDI by the <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>noteon</span></span> procedure, and deactivated
by <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>noteoff</span></span>. Each of these calls may
take:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style='text-indent:-18.0pt;page-break-after:
avoid;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo21'><![if !supportLists]><span style='font-family:
Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>A Port</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;page-break-after:
avoid;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo21'><![if !supportLists]><span style='font-family:
Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>A time</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;page-break-after:
avoid;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo21'><![if !supportLists]><span style='font-family:
Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>A channel</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;page-break-after:
avoid;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo21'><![if !supportLists]><span style='font-family:
Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>A note</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo21'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>A volume</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Each We will go over each of these parameters separately.
The time to play will be discussed below. For now, it can be zero, which means
&quot;now&quot;. The channel is the instrument type to play it to, for
instance, a piano, or an organ, or a tuba. The note is the logical note number
we saw above, one of the 128 MIDI notes. The volume gives the volume the
particular note is to be played at. This might seem odd that we can control
each note, but this is like a real instrument. A piano note can be louder if
hit harder.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>A note can either last forever, until we turn it off with
noteoff, or it can stop on its own. For example, an organ plays as long as you
hold the key down, but a string instrument plays a note when you pluck the
string, then dies away. noteoff need not be used for these instruments, but can
still be used to cause the note to be &quot;clipped&quot; off early, much as if
the player put a hand on the string to stop it. Similarly, a noteon can be used
to restart the note, even while it is playing.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442774"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>I.2<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Channels and Instruments</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code>type channel<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>=
1..16;<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>{ channel number }</p>

<p class=code><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>     </span>instrument = 1..128; {
instrument number }</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>MIDI has from 1 to 16 logical channels, indexed by a logical
channel number. Although there are 128 instruments, you can only play 16 of them
at any one time. To play an instrument, it must be assigned to a channel. This
is done with <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>instchange.</span></span> The instruments we
can choose from are:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code>{ Standard GM instruments }</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>{ Piano }</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>inst_acoustic_grand<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>     </span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>   </span>= 1;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>inst_bright_acoustic<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>   </span>= 2;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>inst_electric_grand<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>     </span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>   </span>= 3;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>inst_honky_tonk<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>          </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 4;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>inst_electric_piano_1<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>= 5;</p>

