style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>= 81;</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Percussion instruments always stop themselves.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The same instrument can be assigned to multiple channels. This
allows an instrument harmonize with itself, playing overlapping notes.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442775"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>I.3<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Volume</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The volume can be set for each individual note. It can also be
set for the entire synthesizer port by <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>volsynth</span></span>.
Volume can even be set for each channel by <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>volsynthchan</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The volume is &quot;maxint ratioed&quot;. It exists as a
value from 0 to maxint, where 0 off (no volume) and maxint is full on.It is not
decibel compensated, meaning that maxint div 2 is not half volume.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Balance between left and right can be set for each channel
with <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>balance</span></span>. Its still maxint
ratioed, except that 0 means middle, maxint means full right, and -maxint means
full left.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442776"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>I.4<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Time and the Sequencer</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>MIDI does not have a concept of time built into the
protocol. All notes or events sent to the MIDI port are assumed to happen
“Now”.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sndlib</span></span> has
sequencer support that is used by setting a time on each event call. If the
time is 0, it means to sent the note or event to the MIDI port immediately,
otherwise the sequencer schedules the event to occur at the indicated time.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>To start <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sndlib</span></span>'s
sequencer, the <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>starttime</span></span>,
which starts a 100us counter running (it ticks every 10,000th of a second). Then,
each time is specified relative to that running timer. The current time on the
sequencer can be found with <span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>curtime</span></span>, so the
required time can be specified as an offset from that:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>curtime+10000</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>means a time that is one second in the future.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>This example dumps a “fanfare”into the MIDI port using the
sequencer. It will be played using the time specified in the <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>noteon</span></span> and <span
class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>noteoff</span></span> calls.</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>program p;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>uses sndlib;</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>const second = 10000;<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>           </span>{ one second }</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>      </span>osec<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>= second div 8;<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>{ 1/8 second }</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>begin</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>starttime; { start sequencer }</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>noteon(synth_out,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>0,<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>           </span>1, note_c+octave_6, maxint);</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>noteoff(synth_out, curtime+osec*2,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span>1, note_c+octave_6, maxint);</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>noteon(synth_out,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span>curtime+osec*3,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>1,
note_d+octave_6, maxint);</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>noteoff(synth_out, curtime+osec*4,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span>1, note_d+octave_6, maxint);</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>noteon(synth_out,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span>curtime+osec*5,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>1,
note_e+octave_6, maxint);</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>noteoff(synth_out, curtime+osec*6,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span>1, note_e+octave_6, maxint);</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>noteon(synth_out,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span>curtime+osec*7,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>1,
note_f+octave_6, maxint);</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>noteoff(synth_out, curtime+osec*8,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span>1, note_f+octave_6, maxint);</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>noteon(synth_out,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span>curtime+osec*9,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>1,
note_e+octave_6, maxint);</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>noteoff(synth_out, curtime+osec*10, 1, note_e+octave_6, maxint);</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>noteon(synth_out,<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span>curtime+osec*11, 1, note_d+octave_6, maxint);</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  
</span>noteoff(synth_out, curtime+osec*13, 1, note_d+octave_6, maxint);</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>end.</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The fanfare plays, and your program goes on to other work,
or you can wait for the sequenced time to pass by setting a timer to the time
required to finish it.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>If you output a note (or other action) with a 0 time while
the sequencer is running, it will still occur immediately. Time 0 always means
&quot;now&quot;. The sequencer is a &quot;flow through&quot; model. You can
time actions and notes with the sequencer, or do it yourself, or any
combination thereof.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>When the sequencer is no longer required, stoptime stops it.
Doing that can save processor time, and probably free up system timers.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442777"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>I.5<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Effects</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>There are many effects in MIDI that can be applied to output
notes. However, there is no requirement for the system to implement them. In
fact, few of the effects are implemented on most computer sound cards or
software synthesizers.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>attack</span></span> adjusts
the &quot;attack time&quot; of each note.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>release</span></span> adjusts
the release or &quot;decay&quot; time of the note.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>reverb</span></span> sets the
amount of reverberation.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>vibrato </span></span>sets
the tremulo.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>chorus</span></span> sets the
tremulo.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>phaser</span></span> sets the
tremulo.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>brightness</span></span> sets
the tremulo.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>timbre</span></span> sets the
tremulo.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>aftertouch</span></span> sets
the tremulo</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>pressure</span></span> sets
the tremulo.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>legato</span></span> sets the
tremulo.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=referenceChar><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>portamento</span></span> sets
the tremulo.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Some missing effects can be simulated by other means. As an
example, <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>release</span></span> control can be emulated
by putting the instrument to control in its own channel, sounding the note,
then lowering the volume in steps until 0, then turning the note off.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442778"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>I.6<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Pitch Changes</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>If we need a frequency that is not exactly on a note, we can
&quot;bend&quot; the pitch with <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>pitch</span></span>.
The pitch change is none for 0, and by default, one note up or down. In other
words, the default pitch change range is one note up or down. A D note can be
bent downwards to C, or upwards to E. The term &quot;bend&quot; comes from
bending a string to change the note.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The default range of pitch changes can also be changed, by <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>pitchrange</span></span>. The range is a
ratioed 0..maxint. 0 means no pitch range at all (disabled), and <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span> means the full 128 notes worth
of pitch range. What you pick up with total range, you lose in fine control. If
the pitch range is <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>maxint</span></span>, each
step of pitch change is going to be very coarse.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442779"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>I.7<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Prerecorded MIDI</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>We don't have to make all our MIDI commands on the fly. In
fact, we can forget doing any MIDI, and just play back prerecorded MIDI files
with <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>playsynth</span></span>. The format is system
defined. Note that even though the prerecorded MIDI file has its own timing, it
is played relative to the clock start position that is indicated for it.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442780"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>I.8<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Waveform Files</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Waveform files are how we get arbitrary sounds into the
computer. Anything, for any length, can be played via the waveform files.
Waveform outputs go out via their own ports separate from MIDI ports. Like
MIDI, however, they are selected via logical numbers from 1 to n, where n is
the maximum number of waveform output devices on the computer. The total number
of waveform devices present in the system can be found via waveout. By
convention, the normal wave output device is 1.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Waveform devices must be opened and closed individually.
They are opened with <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>openwaveout</span></span>,
and closed with <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>closewaveout</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>A waveform file is played with playwave. Waveform files are
usually very system dependent, so the exact format of the file will be
different for different systems.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>As with MIDI files, waveforms have their own timing, and are
simply played relative to the indicated start time.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The playback volume for waveform files is adjusted
separately from MIDI with the <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>volwave</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>It is possible that the implementation will only be able to
play one waveform file at a time. In this case, the behavior will be to stop
any currently playing waveform file and start the new one, if a new waveform
play is ordered before the previous one has finished. High quality
implementation will be capable of playing multiple waveform files at once,
typically via mixing of the files.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442781"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>I.9<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>Functions and Procedures in sndlib</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure starttime;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Start time for sequencer. Starts
the sequencer running. If the sequencer is already running, it will be
restarted at 0.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure stoptime;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Stop sequencer. Halts the
sequencer timer, and releases it.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function curtime: integer;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Get current sequencer time.
Returns the current sequencer time, in 100 Microsecond counts. The count is
guaranteed not to wrap for 24 hours.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function synthout: integer;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Find number of output
synthesizers. Returns the total output synthesizers in the system.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure opensynthout(p:
integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Open output synthesizer. Opens
the output synthesizer by the logical number <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
where p is 1..synthout.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure closesynthout(p:
integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Close output synthesizer. Closes
the output synthesizer by the logical number <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure noteon(p, t:
integer; c: channel; n: note; v: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Start note. Starts a note for synthesizer
<span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, in channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, with note n, and 0..maxint
ratioed volume <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>v</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure noteoff(p, t:
integer; c: channel; n: note; v: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Stop note. Stops a note for
synthesizer <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, in channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, with note, and 0..maxint
ratioed volume <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>v</span></span>. <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>v</span></span> is usually ignored on a
noteoff.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure instchange(p, t:
integer; c: channel; i: instrument);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Change instrument. Changes the
instrument assigned to a channel, for output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to instrument <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>i</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure attack(p, t:
integer; c: channel; at: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set attack time. Sets the attack
time for synthesizer output port p, at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>,
for channel <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed time at.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure release(p, t:
integer; c: channel; rt: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set release time. Sets the
release time for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed time at.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure legato(p, t:
integer; c: channel; b: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set legato. Sets legato mode on
or off, for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to on/off value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>b</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure portamento(p, t:
integer; c: channel; b: boolean);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set portamento. Sets portamento
mode on or off, for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel c, to on/off value
<span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>b</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure vibrato(p, t:
integer; c: channel; v: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set vibrato. Sets vibrato amount,
for synthesizer output port p, at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>,
for channel <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>v</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure volsynthchan(p, t:
integer; c: channel; v: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set volume for channel. Sets
volume for channel, for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>v</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure porttime(p, t:
integer; c: channel; v: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set portamento time. Sets
portamento time, for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>v</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure balance(p, t:
integer; c: channel; b: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set channel balance. Sets the
right left balance for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to -maxint..maxint ratioed value.
-maxint is full left, maxint is full right, and 0 is centered.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure pan(p, t: integer;
c: channel; b: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set channel pan. Sets the right
left pan for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to -maxint..maxint ratioed
value. -maxint is full left, maxint is full right, and 0 is centered.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure timbre(p, t:
integer; c: channel; tb: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set timbre. Sets timbre amount,
for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, at time <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>tb</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure brightness(p, t:
integer; c: channel; b: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set brightness. Sets brightness
amount, for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>b</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure reverb(p, t:
integer; c: channel; r: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set reverb. Sets reverb amount,
for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, at time <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>r</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure tremulo(p, t:
integer; c: channel; tr: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set tremulo. Sets tremulo amount,
for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, at time <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>tr</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure chorus(p, t:
integer; c: channel; cr: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set chorus. Sets chorus amount,
for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, at time <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>cr</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure celeste(p, t:
integer; c: channel; ce: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set celeste. Sets celeste amount,
for synthesizer output port p, at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>,
for channel <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>ce</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure phaser(p, t:
integer; c: channel; ph: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set phaser. Sets phaser amount,
for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, at time <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>ph</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure aftertouch(p, t:
integer; c: channel; n: note; at: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set aftertouch. Sets aftertouch
amount, for synthesizer output port p, at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>,
for channel <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>at</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure pressure(p, t:
integer; c: channel; n: note; pr: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set pressure. Sets pressure
amount, for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>pr</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure pitch(p, t:
integer; c: channel; pt: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set pitch bend. Sets the pitch
&quot;bend&quot;, or change amount, for synthesizer output port <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, at time <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to -maxint..maxint ratioed
value <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>pt</span></span>. <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>pt</span></span>
value is -maxint for full down range, maxint for full up range, and 0 for
neutral (on note) pitch. The amount of pitch range is set by the ptichrange
procedure, and defaults to one note down and one note up.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure pitchrange(p, t:
integer; c: channel; v: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set pitch bend range. Sets the
total amount of pitch change that can be reached by the pitch command, for
synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, at time <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>v</span></span>. 0 disables the pitch command,
and maxint allows it to reach all 128 notes of MIDI. Note that increasing the
range of the pitch command decreases its resolution.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure mono(p, t: integer;
c: channel; ch: integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set mono mode. Sets mono mode for
synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, at time <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>, for the number of channels <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>ch</span></span>. See MIDI specification for
details.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure poly(p, t: integer;
c: channel);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Set polyphonic mode. Sets
polyphonic mode for synthesizer output port <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, for channel <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>c</span></span>. Reverses the effect of a mono
operation.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure playsynth(p, t:
integer; sf: string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Play MIDI synthesizer file. Plays
the MIDI instructions from the file by the name in <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sf</span></span>,
for output synthesizer <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, at time <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>function waveout: integer;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Find number of waveform output
files. Returns the total number of waveform files in the system.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure openwaveout(p:
integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Open waveform device. Opens the
logical waveform device <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, where <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span> is 1..<span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>waveout</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure closewaveout(p:
integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Close waveform device. Closes the
logical waveform device <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure playwave(p, t:
integer; sf: string);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Play waveform file. Plays the
waveform file by the name <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>sf</span></span>, for output
waveform device <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>, at time <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'>procedure volwave(p, t, v:
integer);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='page-break-after:avoid'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:21.6pt'>Set waveform volume. Sets the
output waveform device volume for logical device <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>p</span></span>,
at time <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>t</span></span>, to 0..maxint ratioed value <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>v</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:10.0pt;line-height:115%'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

</div>

<span style='font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:"Times New Roman","serif";
mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-theme-font:
minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:
AR-SA'><br clear=all style='page-break-before:right;mso-break-type:section-break'>
</span>

<div class=Section13>

<p class=MsoHeading7><a name="_Toc251442782"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>J<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Annex
J: Networking Library</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>netlib</span></span> gives Pascaline
the ability to transfer data over a network such as the internet. It does this
by connecting standard Pascal files to network resources. Because of the use of
standard file mechanisims, few added calls are needed.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>To open a new network connection, <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>opennet</span></span> is used. To close network
connections, the standard Pascaline <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>close</span></span>
is used. <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>opennet</span></span> uses an address/port pair
to indicate the network address of the server, and the port within the server.
The address of a server, as determined from its name in characters, is found
with <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>addrnet</span></span>.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>When a remote network port is opened, netlib treats the
connection as a pair of communications channels, one going to, and one coming
from, the remote resource. This makes it easer to use the standard idea in
Pascal of a file having a read or write mode.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442783"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>J.1<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Functions
and Procedures in netlib</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>procedure opennet(var infile, outfile: file; addr: lcardinal;
port: lcardinal);</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>The server is indicated by a
logical address number <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>addr</span></span>, whose exact
meaning and format is dictated by the network itself. A logical port number <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>port</span></span> selects which resource
within the server is being accessed. For the internet, this is a series of
fixed constants that give the exact service being asked of the far server.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>When a network link is opened,
the input coming from the far server is connected to the <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>infile</span></span> of the <span
class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>opennet</span></span> call, and the output to
be sent to the far side is connected to the <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>outfile</span></span>.
These files establish two way communication with the far server.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>procedure addrnet(name: string; var addr: integer); forward;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>addrnet</span></span>
takes the logical name of a server in string <span class=ReferenceChar0><span
style='mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>name</span></span>
and finds the address number <span class=ReferenceChar0><span style='mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi'>addr</span></span> for it. Such
names are formatted according to the needs of the network. In the internet, such
names consist of the characters:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'>Network connections are ended by
the end of the program, or by using the standard file close() procedure on
either of the in or out files of the connection.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:10.0pt;line-height:115%'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

</div>

<span style='font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:"Times New Roman","serif";
mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-theme-font:
minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:
AR-SA'><br clear=all style='page-break-before:right;mso-break-type:section-break'>
</span>

<div class=Section14>

<p class=MsoHeading7><a name="_Toc251442784"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>K<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Annex
K: Character sets</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Like Pascal, Pascaline has no standard character set
representation. Individual characters can be any size, and the mapping of
character numerical values to character gliphs or figures is entirely system
dependent.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The character set used must provide all of the characters in
the word-symbols and special symbols sections listed above, with the addition
of a space.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>This annex describes two different character sets that are
commonly used with Pascaline, the ISO 8859-1 and ISO 10646 sets. For the
purposes of this annex, it is assumed that users of alternative ISO 8859 code
pages will be migrating to the ISO 10646 standard (see below).</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442785"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>K.1<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>ISO
8859-1 Character Set Encodings</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Pascaline itself uses only the lower page ASCII codes, which
are common to all ISO 8859 pages, and only uses a subset of those</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The ISO 8859-1 characters require a set of 256 elements to
be able to represent the declaration:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=Code0>set of char;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442786"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>K.2<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>ISO
10646 Character Set Encodings</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The ISO 10646 or Unicode character standard specifies up to
32 bits of character values. The two variations in common use are UCS-2 and
UCS-4.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code>Variant<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>Bits<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>set of char requirement</p>

<p class=code>--------------------------------------</p>

<p class=code>UCS-2<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>16<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>8192 bits</p>

<p class=code>UCS-4<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>32<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>536870912 bits</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The exact format of a character under the Unicode system is
system dependent. It commonly varies according to if the machine implemented on
arranges its bytes from most significant to least (so called &quot;big
endian&quot;), or from least significant to most (so called &quot;little
endian&quot;).</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Unicode uses the first 0 to 127 character values to
represent the ASCII (or ISO 646) character set. It uses the first 0 to 255
values to represent the 8859-1 or latin-1 character set. Unicode also includes
all of the other parts of the ISO 8859 code pages in higher value codes.
Unicode is designed to be a functional replacement for the ISO 8859 family.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442787"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>K.3<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Unicode
text file I/O</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>When considering Unicode formats, it is necessary to
consider both the internal memory format, and the form as written and read from
Pascal text files. In the case of Unicode, they are not necessarily the same.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>There are several in-file possible text representations for
Unicode. The most common are:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>Name<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>     </span>Bits<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>   
</span>Endian mode</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>-------------------------------------</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>UTF-8<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>8<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>      
</span>None</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>UTF-16<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>   </span>16<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>     
</span>Big or little endian</p>

<p class=code>UTF-32<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>   </span>32<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>      </span>Big or little endian</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Although Unicode represents up to 32 bits of character code
information, it is possible to represent all of these codes in either the UTF-8
or UTF-16 formats due to their use of escapes.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>When big and little endian modes are considered, there are a
total of possible combinations of 5 different unique formats.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>There is no runtime method defined in standard Pascaline to
set or switch between input and output text formats. Such selection is usually performed
by a compile time change that may include special libraries, compiler options,
or some combination.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The &quot;pascaline normal&quot; or suggested default format
for text file I/O, is UTF-8. UTF-8 has the following special advantages:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l19 level1 lfo14'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>1.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>It is compact. It represents the most common
characters in the fewest number of bits.</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l19 level1 lfo14'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>2.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>It is downward compatible with ASCII or ISO 646.
When a text file consists entirely of ASCII characters, the file will be
identical to an ASCII file.</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l19 level1 lfo14'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>3.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>It does not have more than one endian mode.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>To be fair, UTF-8 also has disadvantages:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo15'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>1.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>When representing files whose contents are
mainly outside the 0-255 code range, it may actually increase the net size of
the text file.</p>

<p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style='text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo15'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><span
style='mso-list:Ignore'>2.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]>It moves the ISO 8859-1 128-255 code range
characters outside of the 8 bit range, making text files containing such
characters possibly larger.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Use of UTF-8 makes it possible for Pascaline compilers that
allow both Unicode and ISO 8859 support to switch character set modes and still
keep the same text file format.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoHeading8><a name="_Toc251442788"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>K.4<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Use
of different character sets</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Pascaline is designed to use only one character set at a
time. There is no built in system to represent more than one character set type
at once, nor to switch between character set types at runtime. The
configuration for character set is done as a compile time option.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:10.0pt;line-height:115%'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

</div>

<span style='font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:"Times New Roman","serif";
mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-theme-font:
minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:
AR-SA'><br clear=all style='page-break-before:right;mso-break-type:section-break'>
</span>

<div class=Section15>

<p class=MsoHeading7><a name="_Toc251442789"><![if !supportLists]><span
style='mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;text-decoration:
none;text-underline:none'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>L<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]>Annex
L: Character escapes</a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Pascaline, like Pascal, does not specify a particular
character set. However, the most common implementations of character sets, are ISO
8859-1, and Unicode with representations from ISO 10646. All of these character
codes have ASCII as a subset. Not required, but suggested for standard
Pascaline implementations are character escape sequences. The purpose of a
character escape sequence is to allow access to non-printable characters, also known
as &quot;control characters&quot; within these character sets. Additionally,
there may be characters that, while they are printable, cannot be represented in
program source without a particular font or character set loaded into the host
operating system. In this case, character escapes allow access to these
character by character code number.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The appearence of an escape within a character string is
indicated by the ‘\’ character. Following the ‘\’ character is one of:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>&lt;number&gt;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>&lt;control-identifier&gt;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>&lt;char&gt;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The last construct simply means that the meaning of any character,
including backslash itself, can be &quot;forced&quot; by prefacing it with a
backslash. The backslash itself must appear via a &quot;backslash image&quot;
of ‘\’.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The &lt;number&gt; can be any valid character sequence code.
High quality Pascaline implementations will allow '$', '&amp;' or '%' radix
marked numbers to appear after the backslash character. Examples are:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>The digits that constitute the character are limited by
radix and number of digits. That is, any digit outside of the radix of the
number will terminate the escape sequence. For example:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Gives an octal character escape of &quot;01&quot;, followed
by the character ‘8’, because 8 is beyond the octal radix.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Similarly, only as many digits as are needed to form a character
in the current character set of the compiler are used:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<div style='mso-element:para-border-div;border:none;border-bottom:double windowtext 2.25pt;
padding:0cm 0cm 1.0pt 0cm'>

<p class=code style='border:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:double windowtext 2.25pt;
padding:0cm;mso-padding-alt:0cm 0cm 1.0pt 0cm'><span lang=ES-CO
style='mso-ansi-language:ES-CO'>Base<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>        
</span>ISO 8859-1 <span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>UNICODE 16 bit<o:p></o:p></span></p>

</div>

<p class=code><span lang=ES-CO style='mso-ansi-language:ES-CO'>Decimal<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>      </span>3 digits<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>5 digits<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=code><span lang=ES-CO style='mso-ansi-language:ES-CO'>Octal<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>        </span>3 digits<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>6 digits<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=code><span lang=ES-CO style='mso-ansi-language:ES-CO'>Hexadecimal<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>2 digits<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>4 digits<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=code>Binary <span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>      </span>8 digits<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span>16 digits</p>

<p class=code><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>So for example:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>is not the character for $45, but the character value $00
followed by the characters &quot;45&quot;. Leading zeros are not discarded in
numbers.</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>It is possible for the escape sequence to be ambiguous. In
this case, the backslash character must also be used as a terminator:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Is ambiguous if the desired string is 'The number is '
followed by '12', so use instead:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Control identifiers give easy access to control codes in the
ISO 8859-1 character set. For ISO 8859-1, they are:</p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>NUL<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>       </span>Null character</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>SOH<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>       </span>Start of Header</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>STX<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>       </span>Start of<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span>Text</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>ETX<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>       </span>End<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'> 
</span>of<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>Text</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>EOT<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>       </span>End of Transmission</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>ENQ<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>       </span>Enquiry</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>ACK<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>       </span>Acknowledgment</p>

<p class=code style='page-break-after:avoid'>BEL<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>       </span>Bell</p>

